# Import edges that cross the verifier/subject boundary today, each with the reason it exists.
# Format: `importer -> imported  # reason`. Checked by scripts/ci/verifier_boundary.py (make validate).
#
# This list is a ratchet and only shrinks:
#   * a new crossing import fails the check, and adding a line here is not a fix (with --base REV
#     the check also fails on any entry the base did not carry; CI passes the previous main tip);
#   * a line whose import is gone fails the check: delete it in the commit that removes the import;
#   * entries are keyed by path, so moving or renaming an importer is a new entry: cut the import first.
#
# Imports inside code strings that the verifier hands to a subprocess count too.
# The sides are defined in the script: verifier = server/zerg/qa/** plus the canary script,
# neutral = server/zerg/provider_contract/** (none yet), subject = the rest of server/zerg/.
# Seeded from main at 018eca869. Design: control-plane docs/specs/provider-factory-findings-loop.md,
# 3.2 and 3.3a.

